{"schema":2,"commit":"827eb1585501c6cd6978b8d82981533e16062f75","branch":"main","base_sha":"8f687f9de9348cafbd1048ad15e5c381b08526a7","message":"fix: rename the dev Electron executable so the Dock stops saying Electron\n\nCFBundleName, CFBundleDisplayName, and a unique bundle ID were not enough. Every\nsystem API reported the right name — LaunchServices returned LSDisplayName\n\"Panea\" and NSRunningApplication.localizedName was \"Panea\" — yet the Dock tile\nstill read Electron on hover.\n\nmacOS names an application that was launched by exec'ing its binary, rather than\nthrough LaunchServices, after the executable itself, and it does so before any\nJavaScript in the app has run. `npm run app` execs Contents/MacOS/Electron\ndirectly, so neither app.setName nor process.title could reach it.\n\nBranding now renames that file to Panea, sets CFBundleExecutable, and repoints\nnode_modules/electron/path.txt so the electron CLI still resolves. The rename\nleaves the signature inside the Mach-O untouched, so the app keeps launching\nwithout a security agent asking for admin rights.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018t9iga7qxv4tGRzZDQdBMM","coding_time_nanos":202646572000,"totals":{"added_lines":30,"ai_added_lines":30,"human_added_lines":0,"deleted_lines":8,"ai_deleted_lines":8,"human_deleted_lines":0,"files":3,"tokens":{"input":8,"output":2299,"cache_read":923725,"cache_write":3645},"models":{"claude-opus-5":30}},"by_tool":{"claude":{"lines":30,"deleted_lines":8,"suggested_lines":30,"accepted_lines":30,"tokens":{"input":8,"output":2299,"cache_read":923725,"cache_write":3645}}},"by_gen_type":{"chat":0,"cli":38,"completion":0,"human":0},"files":[{"path":"CLAUDE.md","type":"MODIFIED","added_lines":6,"deleted_lines":3,"ai_added_lines":6,"ai_deleted_lines":3,"lines":[{"start":75,"end":76,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5","gen_type":"cli"},{"start":76,"end":76